{"path":"utility/functional/ranges/greater","title":"std::ranges::greater","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::ranges::</span>greater","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/ranges/greater","section":"utility","kind":"page","summary":"Function object for performing comparisons. Deduces the parameter types of the function call operator from the arguments (but not the return type).","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/functional\">&lt;functional&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> greater<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Function object for performing comparisons. Deduces the parameter types of the function call operator from the arguments (but not the return type).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Nested_types\">Nested types</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-hitem\">\n<td> Nested type\n</td>\n<td> Definition\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>is_transparent</code>\n</td>\n<td> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional#Transparent_function_objects\">unspecified</a>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Member_functions\">Member functions</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator()</span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  checks if the first argument is <i>greater</i> than the second <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<div class=\"t-member\">\n<h2 id=\"std::ranges::greater::operator.28.29\"><span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::ranges::greater::</span>operator()</h2>\n<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> U <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> operator<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> t, U<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> u <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Equivalent to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/ranges/less\"><span class=\"kw2862\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">less</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/forward\"><span class=\"kw1125\">std::<span class=\"me2\">forward</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>u<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/forward\"><span class=\"kw1125\">std::<span class=\"me2\">forward</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>t<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>.\n</p><p>This overload participates in overload resolution only if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/totally_ordered\"><span class=\"kw2971\">std::<span class=\"me2\">totally_ordered_with</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> is satisfied.\n</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Unlike <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/greater\">std::greater</a></span>, <code>std::ranges::greater</code> requires all six comparison operators <code>&lt;</code>, <code>&lt;=</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>&gt;=</code>, <code>==</code> and <code>!=</code> to be valid (via the  <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/totally_ordered\"><code>totally_ordered_with</code></a> constraint) and is entirely defined in terms of \n<span class=\"t-lc\">std::ranges::less</span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue3530\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 3530</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++20\n</td>\n<td>syntactic checks were relaxed while comparing pointers\n</td>\n<td>only semantic requirements are relaxed\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/greater\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>greater</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  function object implementing <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> y</span></code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Nested types","id":"Nested_types"},{"depth":3,"text":"Member functions","id":"Member_functions"},{"depth":2,"text":"std::ranges::greater::operator()","id":"std::ranges::greater::operator.28.29"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"utility","title":"Utility library"},{"path":"utility/functional","title":"Function objects"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::ranges::greater","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. Function object for performing comparisons."},{"label":"Nested types","children":[{"label":"is_transparent","note":"unspecified"}]},{"label":"Member functions","children":[{"label":"operator()","note":"checks if the first argument is greater than the second"}]},{"label":"std::ranges::greater::operator()","note":"Equivalent to return ranges::less{}(std::forward<U>(u), std::forward<T>(t));.","children":[{"label":"Notes","note":"Unlike std::greater, std::ranges::greater requires all six comparison operators <, <=, >, >=, == and != to be valid (via the totally_ordered_with constraint)…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"Defect reports","note":"The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards."},{"label":"See also"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":172,"codeBlockCount":0}
